# LumOn Surface Cache Test Coverage

## 1. Dynamic lighting history
- [ ] Add reusable controlled-scene tests for closing a doorway and removing a light after the surface cache has accumulated illumination.
- [ ] Verify invalidation and relighting remove stale illumination within a defined update budget, and reopening/restoring the light restores illumination.

## 2. Full runtime orchestration
- [ ] Exercise the production surface-cache renderer lifecycle: initialization, feedback, allocation, capture, relighting, debug-view activation, and disposal.
- [ ] Verify published resources and rendered output across multiple frames, including resource recreation, without OpenGL errors.

## 3. Cache-to-final-lighting behavior
- [ ] Identify the currently implemented surface-cache consumers and explicitly record any missing integration before defining end-to-end expectations.
- [ ] Trace controlled changes in cached irradiance through implemented probe/gather consumers to final indirect-lighting pixels; verify both illumination and its removal.
- [ ] Keep missing consumer implementation separate from test coverage work; do not substitute injected downstream lighting for proof of cache consumption.

Use modular fixtures shared across scenarios. Record executed tests and results when completing each item.
